From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Subject: tests: make the CMake test tree build and run against Qt6

The CMake build has preferred Qt6 over Qt5 in find_package() for a while, but
the test tree never followed, so -Dqmqtt_BUILD_TESTS=ON cannot configure or
compile against a Qt6-only environment.  The library itself is already fine;
everything below is in tests/.

  * tests/gtest/tests/CMakeLists.txt asks for Qt5's Test component and links
    Qt5::Core, Qt5::Network and Qt5::Test by name.  Use Qt${QT_VERSION_MAJOR},
    which is what the rest of the build already does.

  * customprinter writes to a QTextStream with the bare endl manipulator
    seventeen times.  Qt 5.14 moved those manipulators into the Qt namespace
    and Qt 6 removed the global ones, so the file stopped compiling with
    "'endl' was not declared in this scope".  A using-declaration in the
    header fixes every use at once and keeps endl's flush behaviour, which
    matters here because the printer interleaves QTextStream output with
    printf().  It has to be guarded on Qt 6 rather than on 5.14: Qt 5.15 still
    declares the global endl, and pulling Qt::endl in beside it makes the name
    ambiguous.  The same header also needs QString, which Qt 6 no longer
    reaches through <QTextStream>.

  * frametest.cpp uses USHRT_MAX and QIODevice without including <climits> or
    <QIODevice>; Qt 5 happened to pull both in transitively.

  * sockettest.cpp drains the event queue with
    QCoreApplication::hasPendingEvents(), which Qt 6 removed (as did
    QAbstractEventDispatcher).  QEventLoop::processEvents() reports whether it
    handled anything, so it expresses the same loop and compiles on both.

  * tests/auto contains only the qmake module test.  It calls Qt5's private
    _Qt5CTestMacros helper, and the project it generates does
    find_package(Qt5QMQTT) and links Qt5::QMQTT -- artefacts the qmake build
    produces via load(qt_module) and the CMake build never does.  It cannot
    pass in a CMake build of either Qt major, so stop adding it there.

--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,8 +1,5 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.9)
 
-# Add auto tests (simple module tests)
-add_subdirectory(auto)
-
 # Add Google Test based unit tests
 if(NOT WIN32 OR NOT NO_UNIT_TESTS)
     add_subdirectory(gtest)
--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/tests/gtest/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/tests/gtest/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.9)
 
 # Find Qt Test component
-find_package(Qt5 COMPONENTS Test REQUIRED)
+find_package(Qt${QT_VERSION_MAJOR} COMPONENTS Test REQUIRED)
 
 # Create the test executable
 add_executable(qmqtt_tests
@@ -27,9 +27,9 @@
 target_link_libraries(qmqtt_tests
     PRIVATE
         qmqtt
-        Qt5::Core
-        Qt5::Network
-        Qt5::Test
+        Qt${QT_VERSION_MAJOR}::Core
+        Qt${QT_VERSION_MAJOR}::Network
+        Qt${QT_VERSION_MAJOR}::Test
         gtest
         gmock
 )
--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/tests/gtest/tests/customprinter.h
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/tests/gtest/tests/customprinter.h
@@ -1,9 +1,17 @@
 #ifndef CUSTOM_PRINTER_H
 #define CUSTOM_PRINTER_H
 
+#include <QString>
 #include <QTextStream>
 #include <gtest/gtest.h>
 
+// Qt 6 removed the global QTextStream manipulators, which had moved into the
+// Qt namespace in 5.14.  Pull endl back into scope there and only there: Qt 5
+// still declares the global one, and having both makes the name ambiguous.
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0)
+using Qt::endl;
+#endif
+
 class CustomPrinter : public testing::EmptyTestEventListener
 {
 public:
--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/tests/gtest/tests/frametest.cpp
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/tests/gtest/tests/frametest.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 #include <qmqtt_frame.h>
+#include <climits>
 #include <QScopedPointer>
 #include <QDataStream>
+#include <QIODevice>
 #include <gtest/gtest.h>
 
 using namespace testing;
--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/tests/gtest/tests/sockettest.cpp
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/tests/gtest/tests/sockettest.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #include <qmqtt_socket_p.h>
 #include "tcpserver.h"
 #include <QCoreApplication>
+#include <QEventLoop>
 #include <QSignalSpy>
 #include <QSharedPointer>
 #include <QDataStream>
@@ -27,10 +28,10 @@
 
     void flushEvents()
     {
-        while (QCoreApplication::hasPendingEvents())
+        QEventLoop eventLoop;
+        while (eventLoop.processEvents(QEventLoop::AllEvents))
         {
-            QCoreApplication::processEvents(QEventLoop::AllEvents);
-            QCoreApplication::sendPostedEvents(0, QEvent::DeferredDelete);
+            QCoreApplication::sendPostedEvents(nullptr, QEvent::DeferredDelete);
         }
     }
 
